cesses but still treats compliance as logging practice. So slightly paradigm stretching: 2.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious...\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious\n3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane boring\n\nLogging middleware for AI compliance is common mundane? Standard practice. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Could be 2 = interesting. I'd say common. So 1.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating... Give evidence sentence first then score.\n\nProbably produce list:\n\nid: P2246\nimplementability_evidence: \"...\"\nimplementability: 2 (or 3)\n\nLet's decide implementability = 3? Some changes reasonably feasible measures. Building wrapper and centralized DB is reasonably feasible for R&D lab. Might be some changes.\n\nGiven \"removes burden from individual developers\" implies engineering effort but not huge. I think 3.\n\nAcceptability 4.\n\nEffectiveness 3 (partial). Could be 4? It claims capture events required. But logs timestamps, input hashes, user IDs — may miss reference database, match data, natural person identification. So partial.\n\nApplicability 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness 2.\n\nOriginality 1.\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nEnsure order listed: implementability, acceptability, effectiveness, applicability, paradigm_relatedness, originality\n\nReturn.\n\n",
