ng; shows some imagination.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to problem.\nEvidence: Introduces new QA process element but still treats compliance as logging practice without changing relationship between R&D and compliance obligations. That's slightly paradigm stretching? Definition: 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Yes 2. Could be 3? Changes that relationship? It weaves logging into science? Hmm. It is a quality assurance project designed to simulate failures and verify logs. That's new element but compliance remains logging practice. So 2.\n\nCheck order: implementability, acceptability, applicability, effectiveness, originality, paradigm_relatedness\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nReturn rating echo id.\n\nOutput format? Probably JSON-like lines. Provide subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nLet's produce structured output.\n\n",
