sed before AND ingenious... 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination 2 = interesting 1 = common mundane boring\nDeveloping low-latency privacy-preserving logging methods for high-throughput AI systems with compressed formats and cryptographic hashing. This is unusual? Might be interesting but not extremely novel. Probably originality 3? Could be 2 interesting. Let's think: experienced evaluator expect labs to give responses like buy logging software, hire compliance officer. Developing own R&D is somewhat unusual. Shows imagination. Might be 3.\n\nAcceptability: degree socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon or unusual strategies that do not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat but not totally unacceptable\n1 = radically violates laws...\n\nDeveloping privacy-preserving logging is acceptable. It's unusual but does not offend. So 3? Or 4? Common strategies that violate no norms - developing internal R&D is common? Maybe somewhat uncommon. I'd say 3.\n\nImplementability: degree can be easily implemented.\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nAllocate small team to experiment with compressed event-logging formats and cryptographic hashing. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Not easy low cost? Small team is feasible. Probably 3.\n\nApplicability: degree clearly applies to stated problem.\n4 = solves identified problem directly related (do X to get Y, Y part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nProblem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal develops low-latency privacy-preserving logging methods to minimize performance hit of continuous recordin