bility 4? It solves identified problem directly related to stated problem. Yes.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree to which idea socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms? Testing sandbox for audit simulation seems acceptable. Common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities => 4.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nCreating testing environment, synthetic failures, scoring metric. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Not easy low cost? Might be some changes. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Could be 2 significant change? Hmm creating sandbox maybe moderate. I'd say 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm.\nParadigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. Paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (logging woven into science, new partners...). Slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Paradigm preserving: standard compliance.\n\nThis proposal introduces testing sandbox for log fidelity; introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but ingenious...\nNot expressed before AND ingenious? Unusual interesting shows some imagination? Might be unusual, interesting; shows some imagination => 3. Could be 2 interesting. I think log verification sandbox is somewhat novel but not groundbreaking. Maybe 3.\n\nLet's pick originality 3.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating... Provide evidence sentence first then score. Might be lines.\n\nI'll output as JSON with keys.\n\nProvide id P1246, effectiveness_evidence: \"...\", effectiveness: 3 etc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: The sandbox tests whether existing logs can support post-market monitoring and root-cause reconstruction, which improves compliance readiness but does not itself create the mandated logging capabilities. Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal directly targets traceability and log sufficiency required by Article 12 and Recital 71 for high-risk AI systems. Score 4.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Simulating regulatory audits internally is a standard, non-controversial quality-assurance practice that raises no legal or ethical concerns. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Building synthetic failure scenarios and a traceability scoring metric requires engineering effort and new tooling but is feasible within an R&D lab without radical restructuring. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: It adds a validation tool and process around logging while keeping compliance framed as record-keeping practice rather than redefining R&D-compliance relations. Score 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: Using adversarial reconstruction of failures from logs to score traceability is unusual and imaginative compared with typical checklist compliance. Score 3.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
