        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nWe need rating for proposal P2012.\n\nProposal: Human-in-the-Loop Audit Interface. lightweight web portal for experts to review and electronically sign off on AI search matches. Handles identification of natural persons involved in verification. Interface pulls flagged logs from middleware and provides simple approve/reject workflow linked to institutional SSO identities. Every action timestamped and written to immutable audit log. Transforms complex regulatory mandate into streamlined technical workflow.\n\nWe need subscales:\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nStated problem: AI R&D lab subject to regulation must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly.\nProposal addresses identification of natural persons involved in verification, logging, timestamped immutable audit log. Article 12 requires logging events, especially for high-risk AI systems referred to point 1(a) Annex III: recording period of each use, reference database, input data for match, identification of natural persons involved in verification as referred to in Article 14(5). So proposal directly addresses logging mandate and identification.\n\nApplicability evidence sentence: Proposal directly targets the mandated logging of verification actions and natural-person identification required by Article 12(3)(d). Score? 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes. So 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? It handles identification and audit log. Does it solve logging mandate fully? It covers verification sign-off and timestamped immutable audit log, pulls flagged logs. May be partial: Article 12 requires automatic recording of events over lifetime, re