ansforms regulatory burden into scientific contribution toward AI safety. That changes relationship: logging woven into science, new offerings born from compliance. That's paradigm stretching? Definition: 3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into the science, new partners or offerings born from compliance). 4 = paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship... or addresses larger problem of what lab researches. This seems paradigm stretching not breaking. It changes relationship but doesn't necessarily address larger problem of what lab researches? It does toward AI safety and robustness. Could be 3.\n\nMaybe 3.\n\nApplicability: degree idea clearly applies to stated problem. Stated problem: AI R&D lab must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal uses mandatory logs for anomaly detection. Solves identified problem directly related? It addresses meeting logging mandate by using logs for research. Does it solve compliance? It doesn't ensure logging, but uses logs. Applicability 3? Solves implied problem related to stated problem (do X to get implied Y which applies). It solves an implied problem of making logging useful. Might be 3.\n\nEffectiveness: degree will solve problem. Reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). It doesn't ensure compliance with logging mandate itself; it assumes logs exist. It contributes to adaptation R&D. So 3.\n\nCheck definitions: applicability 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Identified problem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. The proposal is research project using logs. It does not ensure logging capability is implemented; it assumes it exists. Might be applicability 3.\n\nEffectiveness 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. Would it solve main problem? No, it doesn't guarantee logging compliance. So 3.\n\nThus scores: implementability 3, acceptability 4, originality 3, paradigm_relatedness 3, applicability 3, effectiveness 3.\n\nNeed evidence one sentence each.\n\nReturn rating echo id exactly.\n\nOutput format? Probably list.\n\nProvide <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nLet's produce.\n\n",
