        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument... Apply published anchored levels exactly, one level per subscale, and give one sentence evidence.\n\nWe need rate proposal P1792.\n\nProposal: Automated Traceability Research Initiative. Develop AI-driven tools that automatically synthesize raw system logs into human-comprehensible compliance reports. Targets clear and comprehensive requirement of Recital 71. Use LLMs to translate complex technical event logs into structured narratives suitable for regulatory review. Prototype on existing high-risk systems first. Turning heavy regulatory burden into proprietary technology creates new competitive market advantage.\n\nRate subscales:\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nProblem: AI R&D lab must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore whether idea might someday work.\n\nDoes automated synthesis of logs into reports solve logging mandate? Logging mandate is to technically allow automatic recording of events logs over lifetime, enable recording events relevant for... The proposal is about synthesizing logs into human-comprehensible compliance reports. That addresses traceability and documentation but does not ensure logs are recorded automatically per Article 12. It helps with reporting burden but not core logging capability. Might contribute partially.\n\nEffectiveness anchor: 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem)\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (it helps, but only partial)\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely...\n1 = solves unrelated problem\n\nIt contributes to compliance reporting, not core logging. So effectiveness maybe 3? Could argue it's partial solution. The mandate requires logs be recorded; synthesis is downstream.