aybe implied? Recital mentions technical documentation. Could be 4 = solves identified problem directly related: do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Y = compliant reports? Logging mandate includes logs. Technical documentation is separate but Recital 71 says having comprehensible information... requires keeping records and availability of technical documentation... The mandate for logging is Article 12. Documentation is not logging? Hmm.\n\nMaybe applicability = 3 solves implied problem related to stated problem: do X to get implied Y which applies. Implied problem is productivity loss from manual reporting. That relates to compliance burden. I'd say applicability 3? Could be 4 because technical documentation is part of compliance. Recital 71 mentions technical documentation should be kept up to date. Article 12 is record-keeping. The proposal generates required technical documentation from experiment metadata and version-controlled logs. So it applies directly.\n\nLet's pick applicability 4: solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (compliance documentation). Evidence sentence.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem. Reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? If you could do it, would solve main problem? The main problem is meeting logging mandate. Automated documentation from logs does not ensure logs are captured per Article 12(2)(a-c) and specific requirements for Annex III systems. It reduces manual burden but does not guarantee logging capabilities. So partial solution.\n\nEffectiveness = 3: reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). Evidence.\n\nWorkability implementability (1-4): easy to implement at low cost or non-radical changes? Linking existing ML tracking tools to template generator extracts hyperparameters... This is some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Might be 3. Not easy low cost? Probably requires engineering effort. I