        "content": "{\"ratings\":[{\"id\":\"P2486\",\"originality_evidence\":\"The proposal describes standard MLflow/DVC version control for model and data provenance, a common practice in AI labs rather than an ingenious or surprising approach.\",\"originality\":1,\"paradigm_relatedness_evidence\":\"It introduces tooling into CI/CD but still frames compliance as logging and documentation practice without changing how R&D is defined.\",\"paradigm_relatedness\":2,\"acceptability_evidence\":\"Automated provenance tracking using established open-source tools complies with EU law and raises no social or ethical objections.\",\"acceptability\":4,\"implementability_evidence\":\"Integrating MLflow or DVC into existing CI/CD pipelines requires moderate engineering effort but is reasonably feasible for an AI R&D lab.\",\"implementability\":3,\"effectiveness_evidence\":\"The system captures model, dataset and reference database versions for traceability but does not log per-use events, matched inputs, or verifier identities required by Article 12.\",\"effectiveness\":3,\"applicability_evidence\":\"Creating immutable links between weights, training data and reference databases directly addresses the Act’s traceability documentation requirement for high-risk AI systems.\",\"applicability\":4} ]}",
